Multiply along each path.

$\begin{align*}P(B\cap A)&=0.3\times0.9=0.27\\P(B\cap A')&=0.3\times0.1=0.03\\P(B'\cap A)&=0.7\times0.2=0.14\\P(B'\cap A')&=0.7\times0.8=0.56\end{align*}$

The four path probabilities sum to $1$.

(b) An article can be published with or without a birth.

$\begin{align*}P(A)&=0.27+0.14=0.41\\P(B\mid A)&=\frac{P(B\cap A)}{P(A)}\\&=\frac{0.27}{0.41}\\&=\frac{27}{41}\end{align*}$

(c)

$\begin{align*}P(B'\mid A)&=1-P(B\mid A)\\&=1-\frac{27}{41}\\&=\frac{14}{41}\end{align*}$

(a) The missing branch probabilities are $P(F'\mid D)=1-0.8=0.2$ and $P(F\mid D')=1-0.9=0.1$.

